Prompt "memory" experiments and ablations
Built a MEMORY section of six distilled failure patterns (join fan-out, NULL-ordering, literal precision, hint adherence, filter-vs-output, rank-then-expand) into the system prompt, derived from a hand-audit of ~400 dev errors. Ran controlled A/B ablations at both greedy and 16-sample self-consistency decoding, with three independent replicates to establish a ±2-question noise floor. Net effect is small but reproducible: +7 questions (~+0.5 pts) at self-consistency, while greedy decoding was flat-to-negative. Separately established that one candidate rule (forcing COUNT(DISTINCT)) actively contradicts BIRD's labels — 83% of gold queries counting over a join omit it — and removed it. Also tested LLM-as-judge candidate filtering and pairwise round-robin selection as alternatives to majority voting; all variants scored at or below plain self-consistency, consistent with published findings that untuned selectors lose to voting.

Qwen3.8-27B RL run
Built the end-to-end training and inference tooling for the Qwen RL run — data conversion to Qwen-native tool syntax, sharded async vLLM inference, pass@k and self-consistency evaluation — and swept 15 checkpoints on BIRD dev. Best greedy result 74.05% (ckpt-35); best self-consistency 74.77% (ckpt-20) with pass@16 at 82.20%. The curve peaks early and then degrades as sampling entropy collapses (ckpt-70 down to 71.77%), which identifies where to stop training in the next run. Pruned checkpoint storage to the top six, reclaiming ~400 GB.

BIRD leaderboard submission
Submission code is finalised, zipped and ready to send. Two checkpoints are submitted with a stated evaluation order, both reproducible from a single command with validated defaults. Added a standalone BIRD-parity scorer, per-stage run manifests and completion markers, a full repository map and configuration reference, and the dev predictions behind our reported numbers so they can be verified without re-running generation. Best dev result 74.58% execution accuracy (self-consistency over 16 samples).
